module Incomplete.Gu02 where

{- INFERENCE GIVES UP WHERE CHECKING SUCCEEDS -- 2 of 4: over the cliff.

   THE SCENARIO.  Gu01's denormalised order-line view, with one more dimension.
   Finance asked which tax treatment each line was booked under, so `taxDim`
   joins on after `currencyDim`.  A one-word change to a working query.

   WHAT A COMPETENT USER EXPECTS.  One more join on a chain that already
   compiled: slightly slower, still a save-and-reload.

   WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS, measured on this file, one JVM, nothing else running:

     $ ERMINE_JAVA_OPTS=-Dermine.useInterface=false bin/ermine \
         core/examples/incomplete/gu02_star_join_7dim_inferred.e </dev/null
     Importing module 'Incomplete.Gu02' (329.58 seconds)

   Five and a half minutes.  The module DOES compile -- this is not a hang and
   not an error.  Gu01, the same definition one dimension shorter, is 11.21s.
   Adding `taxDim` cost 29x.

   THE INCOMPLETENESS.  The answer the solver finally returns is 21 partition
   constraints, three per `join`, and it is structurally the same answer it was
   handed: the super-exponential search is discarded wholesale when the residual
   is trimmed.  Nothing about the query got harder to describe between Gu01 and
   Gu02; only the search did.  Gu04 checks eight dimensions -- one MORE than
   this file -- in 1.97s, given the signature.
-}

import Prelude
import Relation
import Syntax.Relation

wideOrderLines orderLine productDim regionDim channelDim calendarDim customerDim currencyDim taxDim =
  orderLine ** productDim ** regionDim ** channelDim ** calendarDim
            ** customerDim ** currencyDim ** taxDim
